---
description: Testing and evaluation conventions
globs: tests/**/*
---
- **Unit test structure**: use `# Arrange`, `# Act`, `# Assert` comments in Python `tests/unittest` and UI `*.test.ts(x)` files (combined lines OK for one-liners)
- **Repo map drift**: structural changes must update root `project.cue` and pass `make verify-repo-map` ([ADR 008](../docs/adr/008-repo-metadata-in-cue.md))
- **In-service tests are unit only** (no `tests/integration/` under services) — HTTP acceptance is `tests/api`; see [ADR 004](../docs/adr/004-no-in-service-integration-tests.md)
- **Default CI is unit-only** — no docker-compose, `tests/api`, `tests/e2e`, or `eval-live`; see [ADR 007](../docs/adr/007-no-live-tests-in-ci.md) (demo/reference project, not production revenue software)
- API Gherkin (`tests/api`): Playwright-BDD against live api/chat/admin; steps use **only** clients generated from `openapi/*.yaml`; `make test-api`; manual / on-demand
- **DeepEval** RAG eval: `make eval-live` (`EVAL_MODE=live`, needs running stack); manual / on-demand — runs the real chat graph
- Eval layout follows DeepEval convention: `tests/eval/test_rag_eval.py` + `metrics.py` + `dataset.json`; run via `deepeval test run`, never raw `pytest` for generation gate
- Goldens are grounded in `resources/` PDFs (not the repo itself). Tier 1 IR: Recall@k, Precision@k, Hit Rate@k, MRR, nDCG@k on labeled `expected_source_file` (`test_retrieval_eval.py`, offline math in `retrieval_metrics.py`). Tier 2 generation: ContextualPrecision + ContextualRecall (0.6) and Faithfulness + AnswerRelevancy (0.7)
- `make eval-live` loads repo-root `.env` so eval uses the same `OPENAI_API_KEY` / LiteLLM settings as the stack
- **LangSmith** prod tracing: `LANGSMITH_ENABLED=true` on chat service (LangGraph auto-traces)
- Test profiles: Dagger functions in `tools/ops` (`test-unit`, `test-all`); `make test-profiles`
- E2E UI: `tests/e2e` (Playwright + Gherkin); not in default CI; `npm test` is fast by default, `npm run test:demo` for slow human-like video
